{
  "description": "Retrieval-quality corpus shared by the server (index-file/retrieval-quality.test.ts, qwen-model lane) and the CLI (kb-local tests/retrieval_quality.rs, qwen_model lane): 25 one-chunk home notes plus the KB's index.md, 20 semantic queries with no keyword overlap with their target, 7 keyword queries. `vectorRanking` is the vector arm's order of every document for each query, recorded from the real EmbeddingGemma 2 (q8_0, 1024 tokens); the non-real-model lanes replay it through a one-hot embedder so CI checks the fusion with the real lexical arm. `thresholds` are the minimum hits per lane: `replay` (recorded vector ranking), `gemma` (real model, qwen-model lanes), `lexical` (lexical-only KB). Earlier baseline: Gemma hybrid hit@1 9/20, hit@3 14/20.",
  "documents": {
    "garden/tomatoes.md": "# Growing tomatoes\n\nStart seeds indoors six weeks before the last frost. Transplant seedlings deep, burying the stem up to the first true leaves. Stake or cage each plant, water at the base in the morning, and pinch suckers from indeterminate varieties. Blossom end rot comes from uneven watering and calcium uptake problems.\n",
    "garden/composting.md": "# Composting\n\nMix green material (kitchen scraps, grass clippings) with brown material (dry leaves, cardboard) at roughly one to three. Turn the pile every week so the core stays hot and aerobic. A finished pile smells earthy and crumbles in the hand after two to four months.\n",
    "cooking/sourdough.md": "# Sourdough bread\n\nFeed the starter twelve hours before mixing. Autolyse flour and water for an hour, add levain and salt, then do four sets of stretch and folds. Bulk ferment until the dough grows by half, shape a boule, retard overnight in the fridge and bake in a preheated Dutch oven at 250 C.\n",
    "cooking/knife-care.md": "# Kitchen knife care\n\nHone the edge on a steel before each use and sharpen on whetstones a few times a year, starting at 1000 grit and finishing at 6000. Never put good knives in the dishwasher; hand wash, dry immediately and store on a magnetic strip.\n",
    "home/furnace-filter.md": "# Furnace filter\n\nThe HVAC air filter is a 16x25x1 MERV 8 pleated filter. Replace it every ninety days, or monthly during heavy heating season. The arrow on the frame points toward the blower.\n",
    "home/water-heater.md": "# Water heater flush\n\nOnce a year turn off the gas valve and cold supply, attach a hose to the drain valve and flush the tank until the water runs clear to remove sediment. Test the temperature and pressure relief valve while you are there.\n",
    "finance/budget.md": "# Monthly budget\n\nFifty percent of take-home pay goes to needs (rent, utilities, groceries), thirty percent to wants, and twenty percent to savings and debt repayment. Review the envelope categories on the first Sunday of each month.\n",
    "finance/taxes.md": "# Tax filing checklist\n\nCollect W-2 and 1099 forms, mortgage interest statement, charitable receipts and childcare invoices. File before April 15 or request an extension with form 4868. Keep returns for seven years.\n",
    "health/running.md": "# Running plan\n\nBuild weekly mileage by no more than ten percent. Three easy runs, one tempo run and one long slow run per week. Replace shoes every 500 to 700 kilometres and stretch calves after each session to avoid shin splints.\n",
    "health/sleep.md": "# Sleep hygiene\n\nKeep a consistent bedtime, avoid screens for an hour before bed, keep the bedroom cool and dark, and stop caffeine after noon. If you cannot fall asleep within twenty minutes, get up and read until drowsy.\n",
    "pets/dog-vaccines.md": "# Dog vaccinations\n\nBiscuit gets the rabies booster every three years and DHPP annually. Bordetella is needed before boarding at the kennel. The vet is Dr. Alvarez at Maple Street Animal Clinic.\n",
    "travel/packing-list.md": "# Packing list\n\nPassport, chargers, universal adapter, medications, two pairs of shoes, rain jacket, toiletries in a clear bag, and a printed copy of the hotel booking. Roll clothes instead of folding them.\n",
    "travel/japan-trip.md": "# Japan trip notes\n\nThe JR Pass covers shinkansen except Nozomi trains. Get a Suica card for subways and convenience stores. Kyoto temples open early; arrive at Fushimi Inari before seven to avoid crowds.\n",
    "tech/backup.md": "# Backups\n\nFollow 3-2-1: three copies, two different media, one off-site. Restic runs nightly to the NAS and weekly to the cloud bucket. Test a restore every quarter.\n",
    "tech/wifi.md": "# Home network\n\nThe router is in the hallway closet. The guest network is isolated from the main LAN. Reboot the mesh nodes if the upstairs signal drops; firmware updates are applied automatically on Sundays at 3 am.\n",
    "car/oil-change.md": "# Car maintenance\n\nThe Corolla takes 0W-20 synthetic oil, 4.4 litres with filter. Change it every 8000 km or six months. Rotate the tyres at the same time and check the cabin air filter yearly.\n",
    "kids/school-schedule.md": "# School schedule\n\nDrop-off is 8:15 at the side gate; pickup is 3:05. Wednesdays are early release at 1:30. Library books are due on Thursdays, and gym clothes are needed Monday and Friday.\n",
    "recipes/chili.md": "# Weeknight chili\n\nBrown ground beef with onion and garlic, add cumin, smoked paprika and chili powder, then canned tomatoes and kidney beans. Simmer for forty minutes. Top with sour cream and shredded cheddar.\n",
    "music/guitar-practice.md": "# Guitar practice\n\nWarm up with chromatic exercises, practise chord changes between G, C and D with a metronome at 60 bpm, then learn one new song a week. Change strings every two months.\n",
    "emergency/contacts.md": "# Emergency contacts\n\nPoison control, the family doctor, the neighbours with the spare key, and the insurance claims line. The water shut-off valve is in the basement under the stairs; the breaker panel is in the garage.\n",
    "home/gutters.md": "# Cleaning the gutters\n\nClear leaves and debris from the eavestroughs every autumn and again in late spring. Flush downspouts with a hose and check that water drains at least a metre away from the foundation. Install mesh guards if the oak tree keeps clogging them.\n",
    "bikes/commuter.md": "# Commuter bicycle upkeep\n\nWipe and oil the chain every two weeks, check tyre pressure (4.5 bar front, 5 bar rear) and replace brake pads when the grooves wear flat. The derailleur hanger bent once after a fall; a local shop realigned it.\n",
    "photo/camera-settings.md": "# Night photography settings\n\nUse a tripod, ISO 800, aperture f/2.8 and a 15 second exposure for star fields. Turn off image stabilisation on the tripod and use the two second self timer to avoid shake. Shoot RAW so white balance can be fixed later.\n",
    "plants/houseplants.md": "# Houseplant watering\n\nThe monstera wants water when the top five centimetres of soil are dry, roughly weekly in summer. The snake plant tolerates drought and only needs water every three weeks. Yellow leaves on the pothos mean overwatering.\n",
    "insurance/renters.md": "# Renters insurance\n\nPolicy number HX-44120 with Northwind Mutual covers personal property up to 30,000 and liability up to 300,000. The deductible is 500. Photograph valuables each January for the inventory and keep receipts for electronics.\n",
    "index.md": "# Home notes\n\nThe household's notes: garden, kitchen, home upkeep, money, health, pets, travel, tech, car, kids, hobbies and emergencies.\n"
  },
